                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Little known fact: Pogo is actually rapper Yeat's favorite game. In the song \"LOCO,\" Yeat says \"Once they see this life, they jump on it like it's-a Pogo.\" Most people think this is in reference to a standard pogo stick, but that is a misconception. That year, Yeat had been playing the game Pogo religiously, grinding every day until he could beat the final world. That is why jumping like a pogo was even on his mind in the first place. Now, if that's the case, then why would he specify *A* pogo instead of just *Pogo*? I'm glad you ask. At the same time, Yeat was ALSO working on his Mario impression. Him saying \"It's-a\" was actually an impulsive tick that resulted from the connection in his mind between \"jump\" and embodying his Mario persona. No matter how many times he tried to say the line correctly, he always impulsively said \"Jump on it like *It's-a* Pogo\" (As in *It's-a me, Mario*) instead of \"Jump on it like Pogo.\" Eventually, he ran out of studio time and had to settle for the most natural sounding take.\n\n\n\nAs for my review of this game, it is a fun, inexpensive physics platformer that will give you a fun challenge. I can recommend it for any fans of the \"Foddian\" genre, although it is not quite a rage game. This is more of a game that happens to be challenging. I can definitely see why Yeat would hold this game on such a high pedastal. At this low of a price, it uses less than 0.000002% of the paycheck from Million Dollar Minion, leaving the rest to go towards iced out watches and illicit substances.",
